---
import { getImage } from "astro:assets"
import directory from "../../../public/assets/pivo-coaches-current.jpg"
import CaseStudyDemo from "../../components/CaseStudyDemo.astro"
import CaseStudyLayout from "../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro"

const previews = await Promise.all([480, 800, directory.width].map(width => getImage({ src: directory, width, format: "webp" })))
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  projectName="Pivo Coaches"
  path="/work/pivo-coaches/"
  title="Pivo Coaches equestrian coach directory with React — Jérôme Schaeffer"
  description="How Jérôme Schaeffer designed and built Pivo’s equestrian coach directory at 3i. Search sample profiles and filter by riding discipline, language, certification, and availability."
  heading="Finding a riding coach with Pivo Coaches"
  image={previews[2].src}
  imageWidth={directory.width}
  imageHeight={directory.height}
  srcset={previews.map(image => `${image.src} ${image.attributes.width}w`).join(", ")}
  sizes="(min-width: 1174px) 1080px, (max-width: 500px) calc(100vw - 40px), 92vw"
  imageAlt="The Pivo Coaches homepage shows a rider filming a horse, a search box for lesson goals, and filters for discipline, language, certification, and availability."
>
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    A rider looking for a French-speaking dressage coach needs to know who teaches that discipline and who has room for
    another student. At 3i, I independently designed and built Pivo Coaches, a public React directory that helps riders
    find equestrian coaches and riding instructors.
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    The public Pivo Coaches directory invites riders to describe what they want to learn or choose filters directly.
  </Fragment>

  <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="narrowing-results">
    <h2 id="narrowing-results">From a riding goal to a shortlist</h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        A rider can describe a goal in the directory’s AI search or start with a specific requirement. Discipline is a
        single choice, while the language filter lets a rider choose several languages they can take a lesson in.
        Pivo Certified and Accept New Students are separate filters. Availability is on when the directory opens.
      </p>
      <p>
        The product filters on the server. The results header reports the total, and the grid loads six coaches at a
        time as the rider scrolls. Riders can change the order from relevance to popularity or browse by newest or oldest.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="profiles">
    <h2 id="profiles">What can you learn before opening a profile?</h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        Each card puts the coach’s name, city, and country beside a short biography. Badges show certification and
        availability, so a rider can compare those details across the shortlist. See More opens the coach’s own page.
      </p>
      <p>
        I recreated that decision in the demo with fictional profiles. For example, Mara teaches dressage in Lyon
        in French and English. You can find her by typing her city, or by combining the Dressage and French filters.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="demo-section" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
    <h2 id="demo-title">Find a sample coach</h2>
    <p>
      Try “Lyon” in the search box, then open See More. Clear the search to compare coaches by discipline, language,
      certification, or availability. This demo matches keywords against nine fictional profiles in your browser.
    </p>
    <CaseStudyDemo demo="coaches" label="Open coach finder" fallback="Enable JavaScript to search and filter the sample coaches." />
  </section>
</CaseStudyLayout>
